WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:03.830
While there aren't too many concrete details
surrounding the Master of the Mystic Arts'

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.580
sequel thus far, there is plenty for hungry
fans to speculate about.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.860
One thing is for certain: Whatever Marvel
decides to do with the good doctor, audiences

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.760
everywhere can expect something... strange.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.620
Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness
may not have started production yet, but that's

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.960
never stopped Marvel from knowing exactly
when a movie will hit theaters.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:27.750
At the 2019 San Diego Comic-Con, Marvel head
Kevin Feige unveiled details on Phase Four

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.910
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe, including
official release dates for all of the company's

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.220
major upcoming projects in 2020 and 2021.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:40.780
This announcement included a May 7, 2021 release
date for the freshly-minted Doctor Strange

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.360
in the Multiverse of Madness.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.520
The decision to move Doctor Strange from November
to May showcases just how popular the character

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.100
has become in the past few years.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.970
While November and the beginning of the holiday
season is certainly a traditional home for

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.720
some major films, May still holds more prestige
in Hollywood circles as the beginning of the

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.820
"blockbuster" season.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.760
Marvel clearly has a lot of faith in this
particular sequel to put it at the forefront

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.760
of its summer 2021 slate.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.000
Who's laughing now, a--hole?”

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.300
Marvel Studios turned heads back in 2014 when
they announced the hiring of Scott Derrickson

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.540
to direct the then-upcoming Doctor Strange.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.300
Before helming the big-budget superhero flick,
Derrickson's career consisted pretty strictly

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.160
of horror fare.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:25.860
From The Exorcism of Emily Rose to Sinister
to Deliver Us From Evil, the director cut

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.220
his teeth on flashy films intended to frighten
moviegoers.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.780
Despite his unassuming track record, Derrickson
turned out to be an astute pick, with his

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.260
eye for striking visuals proving to be an
essential asset to the project.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.460
Doctor Strange has a look and feel that is
unique in the Marvel Cinematic Universe, deftly

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:46.880
blending martial arts choreography and surreal
digital imagery that would make Inception's

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.300
Christopher Nolan blush.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:53.160
In December 2018, Marvel officially brought
Derrickson back to helm Doctor Strange in

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.420
the Multiverse of Madness.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.480
With Derrickson back - and with Benedict Cumberbatch
returning as the Sorcerer Supreme - the future

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.880
of the series is clearly in solid hands.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.780
There may not be an official plot synopsis
for Doctor Strange 2, but plenty of potential

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.580
story hints have been dropped by some behind-the-scenes
people who are in the know.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:16.420
In an April 2016 interview with Double Toasted,
Doctor Strange co-writer C. Robert Cargill

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.090
stated that Marvel felt some of the initial
ideas he and Derrickson had for the first

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:24.760
film highlighted too much of the, quote-unquote
"weird stuff" associated with the character.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.760
To introduce the hero, they reasoned, the
origin story would have to ease audiences

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.200
into his bizarre world.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.760
"Who are you in this vast multiverse…

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.300
Mr. Strange?"

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:43.300
However, Marvel did tell the pair to hold
on to their more outlandish ideas for potential

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.900
future films in the franchise.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.740
Referencing The Dark Knight, director Scott
Derrickson told Den of Geek in 2016:

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.620
"What made The Dark Knight so great was that
the origin story of Batman had been well-told,

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.440
and then it was time to bring in a villain
where you really got to go deep.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.980
And not just the Joker, also Two-Face.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.520
It was a more visceral experience, I'd love
to be able to do that for Doctor Strange."

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:09.980
While on stage at the 2019 San Diego Comic-Con,
Derrickson said, quote, "we're gonna make

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:14.720
the first scary MCU film" which - in addition
to the announcement of a new Blade project

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.440
- raises the following question: just how
horrific will Marvel let their franchises

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:19.940
get?

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.580
Potentially pretty grim, especially considering
the fact that Derrickson has been playing

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:28.800
with the idea of introducing Marvel villain
Nightmare - the demonic ruler of the Nightmare

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.340
Realm - into the MCU.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.420
Spoooky stuff!

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Marvel fans got a pretty exciting surprise
during the 2019 San Diego Comic-Con when it

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.000
was revealed that Elizabeth Olsen's Scarlet
Witch would be joining Cumberbatch and company

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.260
for Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.480
"When you have a strong sorcerer, it also
helps when you have a strong witch - and the

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.060
Scarlet Witch is appearing in this movie alongside
her.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.480
Let's bring Lizzie Olsen back out!"

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.400
Seeing as there are no Avengers flicks on
the upcoming docket - and the fact that her

00:03:56.401 --> 00:04:00.330
own powers draw upon the mystic arts - it
makes sense that Scarlet Witch would join

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.740
Doctor Strange in the horror-tinged sequel.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.980
Benedict Wong has also been confirmed for
Doctor Strange 2, returning as Strange's trusty

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.980
sidekick, a character also coincidentally
named Wong.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:15.380
A prolific performer on stage, screen, and
film, he has been steadily acting since the

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:20.380
early 1990s and has appeared in numerous sci-fi
films, including Sunshine, Moon, Prometheus,

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.900
and The Martian.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:26.620
So we've got a beloved Avenger joining forces
with the Sorcerer Supreme - and we've got

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:30.900
a fan-favorite supporting character lending
his talent to the big screen once more.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:35.770
But the looming question on everybody's mind
is: What about Chiwetel Ejiofor as Mordo?

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.460
"You still think there will be no consequences,
Strange?

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.500
No price to pay?

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.820
We broke our rules, just like her."

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:49.150
The post-credits scene at the end of Doctor
Strange certainly paints Mordo as a villain

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:53.420
and sets him up to be a baddie in future films,
but whether that comes to fruition in the

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:54.810
sequel remains to be seen.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:59.500
The state of the MCU as we know it would be
dramatically different if Stephen Strange

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.900
had not convinced Tony Stark that he was the
key to saving the universe.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.920
For a character who had barely been introduced
a year and a half before Avengers: Infinity

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:11.660
War's release, Cumberbatch's Strange had a
shockingly important role to play in the unraveling

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.700
of the end of Marvel's Infinity Saga.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:18.380
But now that Endgame has come and gone, breaking
box office records along the way, what does

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.140
the future of the MCU hold for Stephen Strange?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.840
Earth has lost three of its greatest defenders
with the deaths of Tony Stark and Natasha

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.320
Romanoff, not to mention the time-travel-induced
aging of Steve Rogers.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.680
Clint Barton seems content to permanently
retire after all of the chaos, and Thor is

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.160
out in space with Marvel's other superteam,
the Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.160
Could Stephen Strange step up to fill the
heroic void left in Thanos' wake?

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.520
Only time will tell.

